{"uid":"66a194aaa5718928","name":"[BUG-XS-004] TC-XS-004 — CORS wildcard * is present even on 401 error responses","fullName":"backend-deep-regression-api.spec.ts:299:7","historyId":"b129211290d82d2343549b58dbd2b11c:843cc37a784806058a7ede977f5d2463","time":{"start":1788766235150,"stop":1788766239177,"duration":4027},"description":"**[BUG-XS-004]**\n\nThe Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * header is returned on ALL responses — including 401 Unauthorized error responses. This means the error body is readable cross-origin by any website.\n\n**What this enables:**\nA malicious page can make a cross-origin request with no token, read the 401 body (`\"Missing Authorization token\"`), and use the distinct error messages (BUG-XS-002) to enumerate token validity from the user's browser — all without any credentials.\n\n**Expected:** CORS headers should only be present on successful responses to allowed origins.\nError responses should not have CORS headers, or should restrict them to the trusted origin.","descriptionHtml":"<p><strong>[BUG-XS-004]</strong></p>\n<p>The Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * header is returned on ALL responses — including 401 Unauthorized error responses. This means the error body is readable cross-origin by any website.</p>\n<p><strong>What this enables:</strong><br />\nA malicious page can make a cross-origin request with no token, read the 401 body (<code>&quot;Missing Authorization token&quot;</code>), and use the distinct error messages (BUG-XS-002) to enumerate token validity from the user's browser — all without any credentials.</p>\n<p><strong>Expected:</strong> CORS headers should only be present on successful responses to allowed origins.<br />\nError responses should not have CORS headers, or should restrict them to the trusted origin.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[],"testStage":{"description":"**[BUG-XS-004]**\n\nThe Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * header is returned on ALL responses — including 401 Unauthorized error responses. This means the error body is readable cross-origin by any website.\n\n**What this enables:**\nA malicious page can make a cross-origin request with no token, read the 401 body (`\"Missing Authorization token\"`), and use the distinct error messages (BUG-XS-002) to enumerate token validity from the user's browser — all without any credentials.\n\n**Expected:** CORS headers should only be present on successful responses to allowed origins.\nError responses should not have CORS headers, or should restrict them to the trusted origin.","status":"passed","steps":[{"name":"Before Hooks","time":{"start":1788766235179,"stop":1788766265966,"duration":30787},"status":"passed","steps":[{"name":"beforeAll hook","time":{"start":1788766235180,"stop":1788766265942,"duration":30762},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"Fixture \"logger\"","time":{"start":1788766265965,"stop":1788766265966,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false}],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":2,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":true,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"Check CORS on Dashboard 401","time":{"start":1788766266152,"stop":1788766267541,"duration":1389},"status":"passed","steps":[{"name":"[BUG-XS-004] Dashboard 401 — ACAO must not be wildcard \"*\" on error response","time":{"start":1788766267539,"stop":1788766267540,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"Bug Evidence","time":{"start":1788766267541,"stop":1788766267541,"duration